<title>FRANCE: Paris air cargo export traffic up 2.2pct in Feb.</title>
<headline>Paris air cargo export traffic up 2.2pct in Feb.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-03-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>February 1997 export traffic from the Paris airports, Charles de Gaulle and Orly, totalled 45,003 tonnes, up 2.2 percent on the same 1996 month Aeroports de Paris, (ADP) figures show.</p>
<p>The ADP's global export traffic in February 1997, by region, with percentage change on February 1996, was as follows:</p>
<p> Domestic		   3,160   up   11.5pct</p>
<p> European Union	   5,618   up    7.8</p>
<p> Non-EU Europe	    1,050   up   11.5</p>
<p> North Africa		 754   down  7.1</p>
<p> Sub-Saharan Africa     3,571   up    2.6</p>
<p> North America	   12,902   up   10.3</p>
<p> French territories     2,056   down  4.3</p>
<p> Latin America	    2,613   up   12.2</p>
<p> Middle East		4,033   down  6.9</p>
<p> Far East		   9,246   down  3.0</p>
<p> Total		     45,003   up    2.2</p>
<p>- Reuters Air Cargo Newsroom Tel+44 171 542 7706 Fax:5017</p>
</text>
